#: apps/tenants/models.py:35
msgid "legal name"
msgstr "razón social"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:41
msgid "tax identifier"
msgstr "identificador fiscal"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:44
msgid "Company tax number (CIF/NIF, VAT, EIN…)."
msgstr "Identificador fiscal de la empresa (CIF/NIF, VAT, EIN…)."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:47
msgid "country"
msgstr "país"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:50
msgid "ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code. Selects the applicable legal rules."
msgstr "Código ISO 3166-1 alfa-2. Determina las reglas legales aplicables."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:53 apps/users/models.py:119
msgid "time zone"
msgstr "zona horaria"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:57
msgid "IANA name. Storage is always UTC; this only affects display."
msgstr ""
"Nombre IANA. El almacenamiento siempre es UTC; esto solo afecta a cómo se "
"muestra."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:60 apps/users/models.py:309
msgid "language"
msgstr "idioma"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:65
msgid ""
"Language the company works in. A person can override it for themselves; the "
"browser's setting is only used when neither is set."
msgstr ""
"Idioma en el que trabaja la empresa. Una persona puede cambiarlo para sí "
"misma; el ajuste del navegador solo se usa cuando no hay ninguno de los dos."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:73 apps/users/models.py:457
msgid "annual leave days"
msgstr "días de vacaciones al año"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:76
msgid ""
"Days of holiday per reference period, in the unit chosen below. Art. 38 ET "
"sets a floor of 30 calendar days, which is 22 working days on a five-day "
"week; the agreement may give more. An individual employee can be given a "
"different figure."
msgstr ""
"Días de vacaciones por periodo de cómputo, en la unidad que se elija "
"debajo. El art. 38 ET fija un suelo de 30 días naturales, que en semana "
"de cinco días son 22 laborables; el convenio puede dar más. A una "
"persona concreta se le puede poner otra cifra."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:88
msgid "counted in working days"
msgstr "contados en días laborables"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:91
msgid ""
"On: only the days the person was due to work are deducted, so a fortnight "
"off costs ten. Off: every day between the two dates is deducted, weekends "
"included, and the figure above should be the calendar-day one from the "
"agreement."
msgstr ""
"Activado: solo se descuentan los días que la persona tenía que trabajar, "
"así que una quincena cuesta diez. Desactivado: se descuentan todos los "
"días entre las dos fechas, fines de semana incluidos, y la cifra de "
"arriba debe ser la de días naturales del convenio."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:98
msgid "reference period starts in"
msgstr "el periodo de cómputo empieza en"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:102
msgid ""
"Month the holiday reference period begins. 1 = calendar year. The period is "
"not necessarily the calendar year: the agreement decides."
msgstr ""
"Mes en que empieza el periodo de cómputo de las vacaciones. 1 = año "
"natural. El periodo no tiene por qué ser el año natural: lo decide el "
"convenio."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:111
msgid "managers see the whole company"
msgstr "los responsables ven toda la empresa"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:114
msgid ""
"Off: a manager reads and resolves only for the departments they were put in "
"charge of. On: for everybody, which is what a company small enough not to "
"have departments wants."
msgstr ""
"Desactivado: un responsable lee y resuelve solo por los departamentos "
"que lleva. Activado: por todo el mundo, que es lo que quiere una empresa "
"lo bastante pequeña como para no tener departamentos."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:121
msgid "pay period"
msgstr "periodo de abono"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:130
msgid ""
"Art. 6.1: a copy of the summary for this period goes out with the payslip. "
"Not necessarily a calendar month --- art. 29.1 ET only caps the interval at "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Art. 6.1: con la nómina se entrega copia del resumen de este periodo. No es "
"necesariamente un mes natural: el art. 29.1 ET solo fija el mes como "
"intervalo máximo."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:137
msgid "record retention (years)"
msgstr "conservación del registro (años)"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:140
msgid ""
"How long clock events are kept. Four years is the floor set by art. 34.9 ET; "
"a longer period needs its own justification, since keeping data because it "
"might be useful is not a basis."
msgstr ""
"Cuánto se conservan los fichajes. Cuatro años es el mínimo del art. 34.9 ET; "
"conservar más tiempo necesita su propia justificación, porque guardar datos "
"por si acaso no es una base."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:146
msgid "security metadata retention (days)"
msgstr "conservación de los metadatos de seguridad (días)"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:149
msgid ""
"How long the IP address, device and user agent of each event are kept. They "
"serve to spot anomalies, not to prove working time: purging them leaves the "
"record intact."
msgstr ""
"Cuánto se conservan la dirección IP, el dispositivo y el agente de usuario "
"de cada fichaje. Sirven para detectar anomalías, no para acreditar la "
"jornada: borrarlos deja el registro intacto."

#: apps/tenants/models.py:155
msgid "settings"
msgstr "ajustes"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:160
msgid "companies"
msgstr "empresas"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:189
msgid "maximum employees"
msgstr "máximo de personas"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:190
msgid "maximum administrators"
msgstr "máximo de administradores"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:191
msgid "maximum storage (MB)"
msgstr "almacenamiento máximo (MB)"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:192
msgid "enabled features"
msgstr "funciones activadas"

#: apps/tenants/models.py:195 apps/tenants/models.py:196
msgid "company limits"
msgstr "límites de la empresa"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:42
msgid "weekly hours"
msgstr "horas semanales"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:50
msgid "Hours a week. See the citation served with the rules."
msgstr "Horas a la semana."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:53
msgid "rest between working days (hours)"
msgstr "descanso entre jornadas (horas)"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:55
msgid "Hours between the end of a working day and the start of the next."
msgstr "Horas entre el final de una jornada y el comienzo de la siguiente."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:58
msgid "weekly rest (hours)"
msgstr "descanso semanal (horas)"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:60
msgid "Uninterrupted hours of weekly rest."
msgstr "Horas ininterrumpidas de descanso semanal."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:63
msgid "a continuous day needs a break after (hours)"
msgstr "una jornada continuada necesita descanso a partir de (horas)"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:67
msgid "A continuous day longer than this is owed a break."
msgstr "Una jornada continuada más larga que esto tiene derecho a descanso."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:69
msgid "break (minutes)"
msgstr "descanso (minutos)"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:71
msgid "the break counts as working time"
msgstr "el descanso computa como trabajo efectivo"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:74
msgid ""
"Only when the agreement or the contract says so. Assuming it would overstate "
"the hours worked."
msgstr ""
"Solo cuando lo dice el convenio o el contrato. Darlo por hecho inflaría las "
"horas trabajadas."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:79
msgid "overtime hours per year"
msgstr "horas extraordinarias al año"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:81
msgid "Overtime hours allowed per year."
msgstr "Horas extraordinarias permitidas al año."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:84
msgid "night work starts at"
msgstr "el trabajo nocturno empieza a las"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:86
msgid "Start of the night window."
msgstr "Comienzo de la franja nocturna."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:88
msgid "night work ends at"
msgstr "el trabajo nocturno acaba a las"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:90
msgid "days to answer a proposed correction"
msgstr "días para responder a una corrección propuesta"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:93
msgid ""
"Days to answer a proposed change before the company may apply it anyway, "
"recorded as made without agreement."
msgstr ""
"Días para responder a un cambio propuesto antes de que la empresa pueda "
"aplicarlo igualmente, dejando constancia de que fue sin acuerdo."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:98
msgid "complementary hours, share of the contract (%)"
msgstr "horas complementarias, porcentaje del contrato"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:101
msgid ""
"Cap on hours a part-time contract may work beyond what was agreed, as a "
"percentage of it."
msgstr ""
"Tope de horas que una jornada parcial puede hacer por encima de lo pactado, "
"en porcentaje sobre ello."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:106
msgid "notice for roster changes (days)"
msgstr "preaviso de cambios de cuadrante (días)"

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:108
msgid "Days of notice before a roster change."
msgstr "Días de preaviso antes de un cambio de cuadrante."

#: apps/tenants/rules.py:112 apps/tenants/rules.py:113
msgid "working time rules"
msgstr "reglas de jornada"

#: apps/tenants/views.py:82 apps/users/serializers.py:238
msgid "That workplace belongs to another company."
msgstr "Ese centro de trabajo es de otra empresa."

#: apps/users/models.py:48
msgid "managers"
msgstr "responsables"

#: apps/users/models.py:50
msgid ""
"Who may read and resolve for the people in it. Only has an effect on the "
"manager profile: an administrator sees the whole company."
msgstr ""
"Quién puede leer y resolver por su gente. Solo afecta al perfil de "
"responsable: administración ve toda la empresa."

#: apps/users/models.py:56 apps/users/models.py:292
msgid "department"
msgstr "departamento"

#: apps/users/models.py:57
msgid "departments"
msgstr "departamentos"

#: apps/users/models.py:92
msgid "address"
msgstr "dirección"

#: apps/users/models.py:95
msgid "municipality"
msgstr "municipio"

#: apps/users/models.py:98
msgid "Decides the two local public holidays."
msgstr "Decide los dos festivos locales."

#: apps/users/models.py:104
msgid "municipality code"
msgstr "código de municipio"

#: apps/users/models.py:107
msgid "INE code in Spain. Names repeat between provinces; codes do not."
msgstr ""
"Código INE en España. Los nombres se repiten entre provincias; los "
"códigos no."

#: apps/users/models.py:110
msgid "region"
msgstr "comunidad autónoma"

#: apps/users/models.py:114
msgid ""
"Decides the public holidays the region sets. Empty uses only the national "
"ones."
msgstr ""
"Decide los festivos que fija la comunidad. Vacío aplica solo los "
"nacionales."

#: apps/users/models.py:124
msgid ""
"Empty uses the company's. Only needed where a workplace is in another zone: "
"in Spain, the Canary Islands."
msgstr ""
"Vacío usa la de la empresa. Solo hace falta si el centro está en otra "
"zona: en España, Canarias."

#: apps/users/models.py:133
msgid "workplaces"
msgstr "centros de trabajo"

#: apps/users/models.py:171
msgid "Full time"
msgstr "Jornada completa"

#: apps/users/models.py:172
msgid "Part time"
msgstr "Tiempo parcial"

#: apps/users/models.py:173
msgid "Reduced working day"
msgstr "Jornada reducida"

#: apps/users/models.py:174
msgid "Training contract"
msgstr "Contrato de formación"

#: apps/users/models.py:175
msgid "No agreed figure"
msgstr "Sin cifra pactada"

#: apps/users/models.py:215
msgid "Read from the roster"
msgstr "Según el cuadrante"

#: apps/users/models.py:216
msgid "Yes"
msgstr "Sí"

#: apps/users/models.py:217
msgid "No"
msgstr "No"

#: apps/users/models.py:222
msgid "Manager"
msgstr "Responsable"

#: apps/users/models.py:223
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr "Administración"

#: apps/users/models.py:271
msgid "Null only for platform superusers on self-hosted installs."
msgstr ""
"Vacío solo para superusuarios de plataforma en instalaciones autoalojadas."

#: apps/users/models.py:295
msgid "email address"
msgstr "correo electrónico"

#: apps/users/models.py:296
msgid "first name"
msgstr "nombre"

#: apps/users/models.py:297
msgid "last name"
msgstr "apellidos"

#: apps/users/models.py:298
msgid "role"
msgstr "perfil"

#: apps/users/models.py:300
msgid "staff number"
msgstr "nº de empleado"

#: apps/users/models.py:304
msgid ""
"The person's identifier in the company's own systems. Acts as a bridge when "
"an external application records clock events on their behalf."
msgstr ""
"El identificador de la persona en los sistemas de la propia empresa. Sirve "
"de puente cuando una aplicación externa registra fichajes en su nombre."

#: apps/users/models.py:312
msgid "Overrides the company language for this person."
msgstr "Sustituye el idioma de la empresa para esta persona."

#: apps/users/models.py:324
msgid "working-time regime"
msgstr "régimen de jornada"

#: apps/users/models.py:328
msgid "Art. 3.b. Decides which limits apply, not just how many hours."
msgstr "Art. 3.b. Decide qué límites se aplican, no solo cuántas horas."

#: apps/users/models.py:331
msgid "contracted hours"
msgstr "horas contratadas"

#: apps/users/models.py:337
msgid ""
"The figure the contract agreed. Empty on a full-time contract means the "
"company's own; empty with no agreed figure means there is none."
msgstr ""
"La cifra que pactó el contrato. Vacío en jornada completa significa la de la "
"empresa; vacío sin cifra pactada significa que no la hay."

#: apps/users/models.py:342
msgid "over"
msgstr "sobre"

#: apps/users/models.py:346
msgid "Whether the figure above is a week, a month or a year."
msgstr "Si la cifra anterior es semanal, mensual o anual."

#: apps/users/models.py:355
msgid "contract starts"
msgstr "el contrato empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:358
msgid "Empty means it was already running when the company started here."
msgstr ""
"Vacío significa que ya estaba en marcha cuando la empresa empezó a usar esto."

#: apps/users/models.py:361
msgid "contract ends"
msgstr "el contrato acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:364
msgid "Empty means open-ended. A date makes it fixed-term."
msgstr "Vacío significa indefinido. Con fecha, es temporal."

#: apps/users/models.py:367
msgid "permanent seasonal"
msgstr "fijo discontinuo"

#: apps/users/models.py:370
msgid ""
"Art. 16 ET: the work comes in periods of activity. Outside them there is no "
"expected working day, and the roster says so instead of reporting an absence."
msgstr ""
"Art. 16 ET: el trabajo viene por periodos de actividad. Fuera de ellos no "
"hay jornada prevista, y el cuadrante lo dice en vez de contarlo como una "
"ausencia."

#: apps/users/models.py:376
msgid "agreed hours"
msgstr "horario pactado"

#: apps/users/models.py:380
msgid ""
"Art. 3.b: the agreed working hours, as text. For example 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Free text because a schedule is not a shape a closed field can hold."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.b: el horario pactado, como texto. Por ejemplo 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Texto libre porque un horario no tiene una forma que quepa en un campo "
"cerrado."

#: apps/users/models.py:390
msgid "night worker"
msgstr "trabajador nocturno"

#: apps/users/models.py:395
msgid ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. A status, not a shift: three hours of the daily working day at "
"night as a rule, or a third of the year. It brings an eight-hour average "
"over fifteen days and a ban on overtime. Leave it on automatic to read it "
"from the roster."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. Es una condición de la persona, no del turno: normalmente tres "
"horas de la jornada diaria en horario nocturno, o un tercio de la jornada "
"anual. Trae un promedio de ocho horas en quince días y la prohibición de "
"horas extraordinarias. Déjalo en automático para leerlo del cuadrante."

#: apps/users/models.py:402
msgid "rotating shifts"
msgstr "turnos rotativos"

#: apps/users/models.py:405
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. The person rotates between shift teams. This does not add "
"limits: it stops the ordinary ones being applied to a changeover, where a "
"shorter rest is lawful and owed back rather than a breach."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. La persona rota entre equipos de turno. Esto no añade límites: "
"evita que se apliquen los ordinarios a un relevo, donde un descanso más "
"corto es lícito y se devuelve, no se incumple."

#: apps/users/models.py:411
msgid "volunteered for nights"
msgstr "adscripción voluntaria a noches"

#: apps/users/models.py:414
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET allows more than two consecutive weeks on the night shift only "
"when the person asked for it. Recorded here because the roster cannot tell a "
"volunteer from somebody left there."
msgstr ""
"El art. 36.3 ET permite más de dos semanas consecutivas en el turno de noche "
"solo si la persona lo ha pedido. Se anota aquí porque el cuadrante no "
"distingue a quien se ofrece de a quien dejan ahí."

#: apps/users/models.py:421
msgid "usual mode"
msgstr "modalidad habitual"

#: apps/users/models.py:426
msgid ""
"Art. 3.e. What a clock event assumes when it says nothing; each event can "
"still record the other."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.e. Lo que asume un fichaje cuando no dice nada; cada uno puede "
"registrar la otra modalidad."

#: apps/users/models.py:432
msgid "date of birth"
msgstr "fecha de nacimiento"

#: apps/users/models.py:436
msgid ""
"Only used to apply the protections the law gives workers under eighteen: "
"eight hours a day, a thirty-minute break from four and a half, two days of "
"weekly rest, and no night work or overtime. Without it those protections "
"cannot be applied, and the system says so rather than assuming the person is "
"an adult."
msgstr ""
"Solo se usa para aplicar las protecciones que la ley da a los menores de "
"dieciocho años: ocho horas diarias, treinta minutos de descanso a partir de "
"cuatro y media, dos días de descanso semanal, y ni trabajo nocturno ni horas "
"extraordinarias. Sin ella no se pueden aplicar, y el sistema lo dice en vez "
"de dar por hecho que la persona es mayor de edad."

#: apps/users/models.py:448
msgid "workers' representative"
msgstr "representante de las personas trabajadoras"

#: apps/users/models.py:451
msgid ""
"Informed when somebody disagrees with a change to their record (art. 4.b), "
"and entitled to consult the register (art. 6.2)."
msgstr ""
"Se le informa cuando alguien discrepa de un cambio en su registro (art. "
"4.b), y tiene derecho a consultar el registro (art. 6.2)."

#: apps/users/models.py:461
msgid ""
"Overrides the company figure for this person. Empty means the company's. "
"Part-time and mid-year joiners are the usual reason."
msgstr ""
"Sustituye la cifra de la empresa para esta persona. Vacío significa la de la "
"empresa. Lo habitual es la jornada parcial y las altas a mitad de periodo."

#: apps/users/models.py:469
msgid "identity provider subject"
msgstr "identificador en el proveedor de identidad"

#: apps/users/models.py:475
msgid "issuer"
msgstr "emisor"

#: apps/users/models.py:478
msgid "admin site access"
msgstr "acceso al sitio de administración"

#: apps/users/models.py:479
msgid "date joined"
msgstr "fecha de alta"

#: apps/users/models.py:487
msgid "person"
msgstr "persona"

#: apps/users/models.py:488
msgid "people"
msgstr "personas"

#: apps/users/passwords.py:76
msgid "the platform"
msgstr "la plataforma"

#: apps/users/passwords.py:78
#, python-format
msgid "Your account at %(company)s"
msgstr "Tu cuenta en %(company)s"

#: apps/users/passwords.py:80
#, python-format
msgid "Reset your password at %(company)s"
msgstr "Restablecer tu contraseña en %(company)s"

#: apps/users/serializers.py:72
#, python-format
msgid "%(code)s is not a region of %(country)s."
msgstr "%(code)s no es una comunidad de %(country)s."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:123
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(name)s does not have a manager profile, so putting them in charge would "
"grant nothing."
msgstr ""
"%(name)s no tiene perfil de responsable, así que ponerle al frente no le "
"daría nada."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:231
msgid "Somebody in this company already uses it."
msgstr "Ya lo usa alguien de esta empresa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:245
msgid "That department belongs to another company."
msgstr "Ese departamento es de otra empresa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:261
msgid "It cannot be today or a future date."
msgstr "No puede ser hoy ni una fecha futura."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:270
#, python-format
msgid "That gives an age of %(age)s, below the minimum working age. %(basis)s"
msgstr ""
"Eso da una edad de %(age)s años, por debajo de la edad mínima para trabajar. "
"%(basis)s"

#: apps/users/serializers.py:274
msgid "That gives an age of over a hundred years."
msgstr "Eso da una edad de más de cien años."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:299
msgid ""
"There is no agreed figure on this regime. Clear it, or choose one that has "
"hours."
msgstr ""
"En este régimen no hay cifra pactada. Bórrala, o elige uno que tenga horas."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:307
msgid "Art. 3.b asks for the agreed hours on this regime."
msgstr "El art. 3.b pide las horas pactadas en este régimen."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:313
msgid "It ends before it starts."
msgstr "Acaba antes de empezar."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:316
msgid "It has to be above zero."
msgstr "Tiene que ser mayor que cero."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:336
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(basis)s: workers under eighteen may not work at night, so the status "
"cannot apply to them."
msgstr ""
"%(basis)s: los menores de dieciocho años no pueden trabajar de noche, así "
"que esa condición no les puede corresponder."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:355
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(hours)s h a week is above the company's %(ceiling)s h. A contract cannot "
"agree past the legal maximum."
msgstr ""
"%(hours)s h semanales pasan de las %(ceiling)s h de la empresa. Un contrato "
"no puede pactar por encima del máximo legal."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:373
msgid "The employee limit for this company is reached."
msgstr "Se ha alcanzado el límite de personas de esta empresa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:412
msgid "A company with this tax number already exists."
msgstr "Ya existe una empresa con este identificador fiscal."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:448 apps/users/serializers.py:461
msgid "Wrong credentials."
msgstr "Credenciales incorrectas."

#: apps/users/views.py:222
msgid ""
"This is the only active administrator. Appoint another one first, or the "
"company is left with nobody able to manage it."
msgstr ""
"Es el único administrador activo. Nombra antes a otro, o la empresa se queda "
"sin nadie que pueda gestionarla."

#: apps/users/views.py:279
msgid "This account signs in through your identity provider."
msgstr "Esta cuenta entra a través de vuestro proveedor de identidad."

#: apps/users/views.py:281
msgid "Reactivate the account before inviting them."
msgstr "Vuelve a dar de alta la cuenta antes de invitarla."

#: apps/users/views.py:337
msgid "You cannot deactivate your own account."
msgstr "No puedes dar de baja tu propia cuenta."

#: apps/users/views.py:403
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(count)s people work there. Move them first: without a workplace they lose "
"their local holidays and their time zone."
msgstr ""
"Ahí trabajan %(count)s personas. Muévelas primero: sin centro pierden "
"sus festivos locales y su zona horaria."

#: apps/users/views.py:458
msgid "The link is not valid or has already been used."
msgstr "El enlace no es válido o ya se ha usado."

